# A trait's implementation is an override of the trait's method: `Store.get` runs the `get` of a type that implements
# `Store`, a choice between them, here `Shelf.get` alone, on the Store the caller calls it on (a value from beyond; the
# trait's declaration has no body to read it). `Shelf.get` builds a `Book` (a unit struct named as a value is a value of
# it) and hands it back at its own moment; the dispatch hands on what its override gave, at its own (law 4, Moment).
# the override's result has the dispatch's own moment: closed, its line into the dispatch is dropped, open it is drawn
